# AN EXPECTED CAST OF A TAIL CALL MAKES NO FAMILY. An expectation that an operation states moves no layout: a Convert [IsExpected] in front of a Return makes no family of its set. Where the Convert stands right in front of `return f()`
# the front end folds it into the tail call's casts, and the scan took every type of a terminator for written: whether two layouts moved hung on where the Convert stood. The casts are looked at one by one, as Convert is:
# the expected L0|L1 makes no family; the written L2|L3 of the second function makes one.
# RUN: link families mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: [L0, L1]
# CHECK: family F{{*}} [L2, L3]
# CHECK-NOT: [L0, L1]

layout L0 module=m0 fields=[{key="a" declared={type=anything} flags=[IsRequired]}] ownFieldCount=1
layout L1 module=m0 fields=[{key="b" declared={type=anything} flags=[IsRequired]}] ownFieldCount=1
layout L2 module=m0 fields=[{key="c" declared={type=anything} flags=[IsRequired]}] ownFieldCount=1
layout L3 module=m0 fields=[{key="d" declared={type=anything} flags=[IsRequired]}] ownFieldCount=1
module m0 path="/main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = NewClosure function=f1
    PropSet v0, v1 key="expected"
    v3 = NewClosure function=f2
    Return v3
}
function f1 name="expected" module=m0 thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="given" [isFreeName]
    v2 = Call v1, -
    ReturnCall v2 casts=[{declared={type=L0|L1 flags=[IsExpected]}}]
}
function f2 name="written" module=m0 thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="given" [isFreeName]
    v2 = Call v1, -
    ReturnCall v2 casts=[{declared={type=L2|L3}}]
}
